     "explanation": "This is Lucilius's mistake in modern form. The Stoic move is not dramatic confrontation or instant rupture — it is **clarity of label**. Either the relationship is friendship, in which case it deserves honest conversation and full trust; or it is not, in which case it should not be called friendship. The unbearable middle — \"friend\" in name, **perversi animi** in fact — is the state Seneca warns Lucilius against.",
