     "explanation": "The four death-letters form one curriculum. **Letter 12** treats each day as a complete life. **Letter 26** uses old age as a dress rehearsal and prescribes a nightly examen. **Letter 70** shifts the measure from length to quality. **Letter 77** delivers the shame test. The unifying argument is that **steady, daily confrontation with mortality** — not avoidance, not morbidity — is the only thing that makes life clear, free, and well-used. Death rehearsed is freedom won.",
