     "explanation": "This is the modern Calvisius Sabinus problem. You have **exposure** and **comprehension** — you can quote Stoic ideas correctly. But you have not yet moved to **practice** — you cannot name an instance in the last week when the ideas changed your behavior. Seneca's warning in Letter 27 is exact: wisdom does not transfer by proximity to wise material, only by use. The cure is to pick one practice from Letter 13, 18, or 26 and **run it tomorrow**.",
